Troubleshooting Common Issues
Database Connection Issues
Problem: Cannot connect to PostgreSQL database during backup

Solution:

# Check PostgreSQL service status
systemctl status postgresql

# Verify database user permissions
sudo -u postgres psql -c "\du"

# Test connection manually
sudo -u awx psql -h localhost -d awx -c "SELECT 1;"
Insufficient Disk Space
Problem: Backup fails due to insufficient disk space

Solution:

# Check available disk space
df -h /backup

# Clean up old backups
find /backup -name "*.gz" -mtime +30 -delete

# Move backups to external storage
rsync -av /backup/ /mnt/external-storage/backup/
Service Interruption During Backup
Problem: Services become unavailable during backup

Solution:

# Use pg_dump with minimal locking
pg_dump --no-password --verbose --clean --create \
  --serializable-deferrable \
  --file=backup.sql database_name

# Schedule backups during maintenance windows
# Use read-only mode during critical backups
Backup Corruption
Problem: Backup files are corrupted or incomplete

Solution:

# Always verify backup integrity
gunzip -t backup_file.sql.gz
tar -tzf backup_file.tar.gz

# Use checksums for verification
sha256sum backup_file.gz > backup_file.gz.sha256
sha256sum -c backup_file.gz.sha256

# Implement multiple backup copies
cp backup_file.gz backup_file_copy.gz
Best Practices for Production Environments
Backup Strategy Recommendations
3-2-1 Backup Rule: • Keep 3 copies of important data • Store copies on 2 different media types • Keep 1 copy offsite

Implementation:

# Local backup
/backup/full_platform_backup.sh

# Copy to network storage
rsync -av /backup/ /mnt/nas/ansible-backups/

# Upload to cloud storage
aws s3 sync /backup/ s3://company-ansible-backups/
Monitoring and Alerting
# Create backup monitoring script
cat > /backup/monitor_backups.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash

# Check if backups are recent (within 25 hours)
CONTROLLER_DB=$(find /backup/controller/database -name "*.sql.gz" -mtime -1)
HUB_DB=$(find /backup/hub/database -name "*.sql.gz" -mtime -1)

if [ -z "$CONTROLLER_DB" ] || [ -z "$HUB_DB" ]; then
    echo "ALERT: Missing recent backups!"
    # Send alert notification
    exit 1
else
    echo "OK: Recent backups found"
    exit 0
fi
EOF

# Add to cron for monitoring
(crontab -l; echo "0 8 * * * /backup/monitor_backups.sh") | crontab -
Security Considerations
# Encrypt sensitive backups
gpg --symmetric --cipher-algo AES256 backup_file.sql.gz

# Set proper permissions
chmod 600 /backup/controller/database/*.gz
chmod 600 /backup/hub/database/*.gz

# Use dedicated backup user
useradd -r -s /bin/false backup-user
